.TH XSHELF 1 "April 2026" "XSHELF" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xshelf, xs, cx \- deterministic Rust-first runtime for repo-aware LLM workflows
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xshelf
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.br
.B xs
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.br
.B cx
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.br
.B ./bin/xshelf
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.br
.B ./bin/xs
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.br
.B ./bin/cx
\fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xshelf
is a repository-local AI runtime and orchestration CLI.
It is Rust-first and deterministic for structured operations.
.PP
\fBxs\fR is a supported short alias for \fBxshelf\fR.
.PP
\fBcx\fR remains a supported compatibility alias during the rename transition.
.PP
Core capabilities include:
.IP \(bu 2
repo-aware command execution and LLM routing,
.IP \(bu 2
schema-enforced structured commands with quarantine/replay,
.IP \(bu 2
context budgeting and capture telemetry,
.IP \(bu 2
task graph orchestration and controlled execution lanes,
.IP \(bu 2
diagnostics, validation, and optimization tooling.
.SH QUICK START
.nf
./bin/xshelf version
./bin/xshelf core
./bin/xshelf doctor
./bin/xshelf health
./bin/xshelf cxo git status
.fi
.SH COMMON COMMANDS
.TP
.B version
Print tool version and source metadata.
.TP
.B core
Show execution-core pipeline config.
.TP
.B help
Print full command list.
.TP
.B where
Show binary/source/log resolution details.
.TP
.B routes [\-\-json] [cmd...]
Routing introspection for supported commands.
.TP
.B diag [\-\-json] [\-\-window N] [\-\-strict] [\-\-actions] [\-\-severity warning|critical]
Non-interactive diagnostic report.
.TP
.B doctor
Environment/runtime checks.
.TP
.B health
End-to-end smoke checks.
.SH LLM EXECUTION
.TP
.B xshelf cxo <cmd...>
Run captured command output and print the last agent message.
.TP
.B cx <cmd...>
Compatibility LLM text-mode command.
.TP
.B cxj <cmd...>
Run through LLM JSONL mode.
.TP
.B cxo <cmd...>
Run and print last agent message.
.TP
.B cxol <cmd...>
Run through LLM plain mode.
.TP
.B cxcopy <cmd...>
Copy cxo output to clipboard.
.SH STRUCTURED COMMANDS
.TP
.B commitjson
Generate strict JSON commit object.
.TP
.B commitmsg
Generate commit message text from staged diff.
.TP
.B diffsum
Summarize unstaged diff.
.TP
.B diffsum-staged
Summarize staged diff.
.TP
.B next <cmd...>
Suggest next shell commands.
.TP
.B fix-run <cmd...>
Generate remediation command list from failure context.
.TP
.B replay <id>
Replay quarantined schema run in strict mode.
.TP
.B schema list [\-\-json]
List registered schemas.
.SH TASK ORCHESTRATION
.TP
.B task add/list/show/claim/complete/fail/fanout/run/run-all
Task graph management and controlled execution.
.SH LOGS AND ANALYTICS
.TP
.B metrics [N]
Token/duration aggregates.
.TP
.B profile [N]
Run profile summary.
.TP
.B trace [N]
Inspect Nth-most-recent run.
.TP
.B alert [N]
Anomaly report over recent runs.
.TP
.B optimize [N] [\-\-json] [\-\-actions] [\-\-strict] [\-\-severity warning|critical]
Optimization recommendations from historical telemetry.
.TP
.B logs validate [\-\-strict] [\-\-legacy-ok]
Validate run-log JSONL contract.
.TP
.B logs stats [N] [\-\-json] [\-\-strict] [\-\-severity ...]
Telemetry health/contract drift summary.
.SH BACKEND AND STATE
.TP
.B llm show|check|smoke|use|unset|set-backend|set-model|clear-model
Manage and verify backend/model selection.
.TP
.B state show|get|set
Read/write repo state in \fB.cx/state.json\fR.
.TP
.B quota ...
Quota probing/catalog/guard controls.
.SH SAFETY
.TP
.B policy show
Show active command safety policy.
.TP
.B policy check <cmd...>
Classify a command as safe/dangerous.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .cx/cxlogs/runs.jsonl
Execution telemetry log.
.TP
.I .cx/cxlogs/schema_failures.jsonl
Schema failure ledger.
.TP
.I .cx/quarantine/
Quarantined malformed structured outputs.
.TP
.I .cx/schemas/
Schema registry.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CX_MODE
Execution mode (for example: lean, deterministic, verbose).
.TP
.B CX_LLM_BACKEND
Backend selection (for example: primary, ollama, llamacpp, mlx).
.TP
.B CX_OLLAMA_MODEL
Model used when backend is ollama.
.TP
.B CX_LLAMA_CPP_MODEL
GGUF model path or llama.cpp Hugging Face repo spec used when backend is llamacpp.
For example: /models/model.gguf or ggml-org/Qwen3-0.6B-GGUF:Q4_0.
.TP
.B CX_LLAMA_CPP_BIN
llama.cpp CLI binary path/name. Defaults to llama-cli.
.TP
.B CX_LLAMA_CPP_ARGS
Additional shell-split arguments appended to llama-cli.
.TP
.B CX_MLX_MODEL
MLX model identifier/path used when backend is mlx.
.TP
.B CX_MLX_PYTHON
Python executable for mlx-lm. Defaults to python3.
.TP
.B CX_MLX_ARGS
Additional shell-split arguments appended to python -m mlx_lm generate.
.TP
.B CX_MLX_MAX_TOKENS
Optional max-token value passed to mlx-lm generate.
.TP
.B CX_CONTEXT_BUDGET_CHARS
Context character budget.
.TP
.B CX_CONTEXT_BUDGET_LINES
Context line budget.
.TP
.B CX_CONTEXT_CLIP_MODE
Clipping mode (head, tail, smart).
.TP
.B CX_CONTEXT_CLIP_FOOTER
Include clipping footer when clipping occurs.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime/processing error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage/argument error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
xshelf version
xshelf llm show
xshelf cxo git status
xshelf schema list --json | jq .
xshelf logs validate --strict
xshelf optimize 200 --json | jq .
man xshelf
man xs
man cx
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cxrs (1),
.BR jq (1),
.BR git (1)
